abstract = {Weyl-type eigenvalue perturbation theories are derived for Hermitian definite pencils A-λB, in which B is positive definite. The results provide a one-to-one correspondence between the original and perturbed eigenvalues, and give a uniform perturbation bound. We give both absolute and relative perturbation results, defined in the standard Euclidean metric instead of the chordal metric that is often used.}
